('ca2393bf-e590-4a57-8d9d-8418a27f1afc', 'BIO-LIV-0125', 'a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a13', 'b0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380b15', 'MCQ', '[{"type": "text", "html": "<p>Statement 1 : The first word denoting the genus starts with a small letter in binomial nomenclature. Statement II : The specific epithet starts with a capital letter in binomial nomenclature. Statement1: Each genus may have one or more than one specific epithets representing different organisms having morphological similarities. Statement II : Lion, leopard and tiger are all species of the genus Panthera. Statement 1 : Felidae consists of genus Panthera and Felis. Statement Il : Felidae is a cat family that comprises of lion, tiger, leopard and cat.</p>"}]', '[{"type": "text", "html": "<p>Refer to NCERT Class 11 Biology: Chapter 1 - The Living World.</p>"}]', 'Hard', 4, 1, 'b', 'grid_2x2', 2024, 'NEET Biology Bank', 'Statement 1 : The first word denoting the genus starts with a small letter in binomial nomenclature. Statement II : The specific epithet starts with a capital letter in binomial nomenclature. Statement1: Each genus may have one or more than one specific epithets representing different organisms having morphological similarities. Statement II : Lion, leopard and tiger are all species of the genus Panthera. Statement 1 : Felidae consists of genus Panthera and Felis. Statement Il : Felidae is a cat family that comprises of lion, tiger, leopard and cat.'),
